;;; A hypothesis rule's template writes a variable that no premise binds, and proposed
;;; nothing, in silence — regression `hrule-assert-var`
;;; (`corpus/regressions.toml`).
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; One fact `(p a)`, and a rule without parameters that concludes the hypothesis
;;; `(open (q ?y))`, whose `?y` its `:match` never binds.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A hypothesis is held to what any conclusion is held to (Q-M1e2.37): every
;;; variable bound on every way its `:match` can hold. `?y` is not, so the
;;; program is refused at load, and every command that loads it exits 1 with the
;;; loader's line (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The program loaded, and the template built no fact for any match, which
;;; the candidate generator skipped: H was
;;; empty and R {∅}, exit 0 on every command, with no word of `?y` (`ein
;;; solve FILE` and `ein oracle FILE` at `2eb483e0`, release and debug
;;; alike). The engine now refuses it at load.

(relation p Node :why "{?3} is a node")
(relation q Node :why "{?3} is a q")
(p a)
(rule h ()
  :match (p ?x)
  :assert (open (q ?y))
  :why "suppose a q, since {?x} is a p")
